EnvelopeExec: SetRevMtx's inverse starts as zero, not uninitialised stack, on MPT_PC
Applied in order by runtimes/gc_wii/mp4/CMakeLists.txt with `git apply`.

ADR 0008, "Gate status after the implementation", decision point 1. SetRevMtx (inlined into
InitEnvelope, called by LoadHSF for every enveloped model) inverts each object's matrix into the local
sp38 and concatenates it into the model's reverse matrices. MTXInverse returns 0 and writes nothing
for a singular matrix, so when the first matrix inverted is singular, MTXConcat reads sp38
uninitialised. On the console that is stale stack too; on PC the stack holds host frames, so the
reverse matrices (read by the renderer and by EnvelopeProc) held bytes of return addresses and moved
with the code layout. sp38 now starts as zero. After a successful inverse the loop still reuses the
last one, which the game computed and every platform computes the same. Unconditional on PC.

